  "finalReply": "Created `/app/config/parser.sh.py` as a bash+Python polyglot:\n\n- Header `#!/bin/bash` + `\"\"\":\"` / `\":\"\"\"` is `:` no-op in bash and a triple-quoted string in Python, hiding each implementation from the other interpreter. Bash block ends with explicit `exit` so bash never falls through to Python code.\n- Both implementations: validate 2 non-empty args, check file exists/is-file/readable, check non-empty (`-s` + whitespace-only check / `getsize` + `strip` check), skip blanks/comments, require first `=` or `:` separator, trim key/value, strip matching surrounding quotes, flag missing separator / empty key / whitespace in key as malformed (stderr + exit 1), last-wins lookup, `KEY_NOT_FOUND` with exit 0 when valid but absent.\n- Supports `key=value` and `key: value` with optional surrounding whitespace and values containing `=`/`:` (split on first separator).\n\nMade executable (`chmod +x`).",
